SUMMARY:The Neon Room at Helium: Kirsten Michelle Cills
LOCATION:Helium Comedy Club\, 1510 SE 9th Ave\, Portland
DESCRIPTION:Kirsten Michelle Cills is a terminally ill stand-up comic known
  for her dark wit\, commanding stage presence\, and unmistakable Philly edg
 e. Performing alongside her oxygen tank\, she transforms personal adversity
  into razor-sharp comedy. Kirsten has headlined clubs and colleges nationwi
 de and opened for Tim Meadows\, Judy Gold\, Mark Gagnon\, and Laurie Kilmar
 tin. She was recently featured at the Big Pine Comedy Festival and the Bost
 on Comedy Festival\, earning “Best of Fest” honors at both.\n\nPLEASE 
 NOTE:\n\nKirsten is a comedian living with Cystic Fibrosis. While we unders
 tand that other individuals with Cystic Fibrosis may want to enjoy her come
 dy live\, the CF Foundation recommends only one person with Cystic Fibrosis
  per indoor space. We kindly ask that if you are an individual living with 
 Cystic Fibrosis\, you please respect these boundaries for everyone’s safe
 ty. Many adults with CF may feel more comfortable taking risks while on mod
 ulators\, such as Trikafta or similar life-changing medications\, however K
 irsten has a rare CF mutation and does not qualify for these new treatments
 \, leaving her still very vulnerable.\n\nIf you have CF and still intend on
  coming to a show knowing these risks\, while we cannot require anyone to d
 isclose their medical history\, we respectfully ask that you email [contact
  removed] to give a heads-up that you will be in attendance. We will make s
 ure to seat you at least six feet from the stage. Thank you for your unders
 tanding while we prioritize the health and safety of all CFers.\n\nManageme
 nt reserves the right to prevent customers from entering the facility who t
 hey deem disruptive or dangerous to other patrons.\nMore info: https://come
 dyatlas.app/comedy-atlas/event/the-neon-room-at-helium-kirsten-michelle-cil
 ls/
